# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/next-2 window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/next-2 and push a tag
# experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch that holds them.
# ONE IMAGE: tp4-next2-1 (B0's image; the default drafter manifest dedf8df6). A tag that already exists is skipped by the build step. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# D-T1: the SAME-IMAGE CONTROL tau arm of D-T5 (the drafter pack's D-T1, re-pointed from its own image to tp4-next2-1). It MUST run before D-T5 on this image: D-T5's C2_TAULAB_PAIR_CONTROL is the run id of THIS job,
# and the pair report refuses runs whose image tags differ (an older control on tp4-drafter-1 would pair the lookup against a different stack). NOTE the run id of this job's workflow run.
# D-T1 (the control arm itself): the CONTROL tau arm: the default drafter (dedf8df6) on image tp4-next2-1. A3 (the calibration: the lanes' 4 x 4k and 4 x 32k prompts, thinking OFF) runs on THIS arm only and must reproduce the
# served drafter's own reference within +/-7%; then A1 and A2. The candidate arms name that run id (C2_TAULAB_PAIR_CONTROL=<digits>) so their step pairs
# them with it. Thinking ON, coding-agent turns from the public SWE-rebench set (A1) and the scrubbed own-session set (A2) as the lab already uses, no customer traffic; the data directory is rig-local and
# read-only to the job (kwork64/taulab/data under the runner's home), checked against its manifest before the container starts. The serving profile is c2-packed-tp4 with the lab's two
# arithmetic-neutral log flags and, for a drafter arm, only that arm's drafter-only flags. Judged PAIRED per turn id by drafter_pair_report.py against the control arm (the GO rule is in its
# docstring and docs/drafter-arms.md): pooled ratio lower 95%% bound > 1.00, no regression in the 80k+ bucket or at p10, identical text, both runs launched clean and asked the same questions; the control A3 verdict is an annotation. Duration (estimate): 90 min (the deadline of 85 min is counted from the container start, the load included). Kill rule: the lab runs A3 FIRST on this arm (whatever order C2_TAULAB_ARMS lists) and stops after it on a FAIL, before A1 and A2, which voids the window's tau arms (the stack, not the drafter, moved tau: re-derive the reference first); a launched-argv problem line (the log shows another arm's marker) refuses the arm before anything is sent and exits 2; the canary or the breaker stopping the lab, or a stall, ends the arm.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset taulab
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next2-1
C2_TAULAB_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4
C2_TAULAB_DRAFTER_ARM=control
C2_TAULAB_ARMS=A3 A1 A2
C2_TAULAB_DEADLINE=85
C2_TAULAB_IN_FLIGHT=8
